FADE IN:

EXT. MOUNTAIN PEAK - DAWN

The sun breaks over a majestic mountain range. Mist rises from the valleys below.

ELENA (40s, weathered but determined) stands at the edge of a cliff, backpack at her feet.

ELENA
(whispered)
Made it.

She pulls out a worn photograph from her pocket - a young boy smiling.

ELENA (V.O.)
Three years. Three years since you asked me to see the world for you.

She sits on a rock, pulls out a thermos.

INT. ELENA'S APARTMENT - FLASHBACK - NIGHT

A cramped city apartment. MARCUS (8, wearing an oxygen mask) lies in a hospital bed. Elena sits beside him.

MARCUS
Mom, promise me something.

ELENA
Anything, baby.

MARCUS
See the sunrise from a mountain. The tallest one you can find.

Elena fights back tears.

ELENA
I promise.

CUT TO:

EXT. MOUNTAIN PEAK - DAWN - CONTINUOUS

Elena watches as golden light floods the valley.

HIKER (O.S.)
Beautiful, isn't it?

Elena turns. A HIKER (60s, kind eyes) approaches.

ELENA
It really is.

HIKER
First time up here?

ELENA
First time doing anything like this.

The hiker sits nearby, respecting her space.

HIKER
Everyone's got a story. A reason they climb.

ELENA
(beat)
My son. He was eight.

The hiker nods, understanding.

HIKER
To the ones who send us climbing.

He raises an imaginary glass. Elena smiles through tears.

ELENA
To the ones who send us climbing.

They sit in comfortable silence as the sun rises fully.

EXT. MOUNTAIN TRAIL - LATER

Elena descends the trail, lighter somehow. She passes other hikers heading up.

YOUNG HIKER
Great day for it!

ELENA
The best.

She pulls out her phone, opens the camera.

ELENA (V.O.)
I kept my promise, Marcus. And you know what? I think I'll keep climbing.

She snaps a selfie with the mountain behind her, smiling genuinely for the first time in years.

INT. ELENA'S APARTMENT - DAY

Elena enters, changed. She sets down her backpack and goes to a wall covered in maps.

She traces a line with her finger - from mountain to mountain, continent to continent.

ELENA
(determined)
Next stop... Kilimanjaro.

She circles the mountain on the map.

FADE OUT.

THE END
